# ============================================================================
# Docker build context (repo root).
#
# Build strategy: every Python image is built with the REPOSITORY ROOT as the
# build context, because the services share a single `uv.lock` workspace. That
# makes this file — not a per-service one — the thing that decides what the
# daemon has to hash and upload.
#
# Keep:  pyproject.toml, uv.lock, services/**/pyproject.toml, services/**/*.py,
#        alembic/**, and any static assets a service needs.
# Drop:  everything below — VCS, docs, tests, runtime data, caches, media.
# ============================================================================

# --- VCS -------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Documentation and assignment material ---------------------------------
docs
*.md
!README.md
AGENTCORE.md
LICENSE

# --- Never ship runtime state or secrets -----------------------------------
data
.env
.env.*
secrets
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.pem
*.key

# --- Python caches / virtualenvs -------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
.venv
**/.venv
uv.lock.bak

# --- Tests and dev tooling (not needed inside images) ----------------------
**/tests
**/test_*.py
**/*_test.py
.pytest_cache
specs
tests

# --- The mock and the web service (not needed by Python service images) ----
mock-ticketing
services/web/static
services/web/*.conf

# --- Node ------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules
**/node_modules

# --- Editor / OS noise -----------------------------------------------------
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.log
